#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157084 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65d40bd9-4d35-5e07-a767-8b2ae6ba559a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Union of Sets Without a Venn Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "99f04ab6-00a0-5ccc-a328-49a85547c4c1" :question/math-academy-id "e-7153" :question/problem "Given the sets $X = \\{2, 5, 7, 8\\},$ $Y = \\{1, 3, 5\\},$ and $Z = \\{2, 4, 6, 8\\},$ find $X \\cup Y,$ $Y \\cup Z,$ and $Z \\cup X.$" :question/worked-solution "The union $X \\cup Y$ is the set of all elements belonging to either $X$ or $Y,$ or both. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X\\cup Y & =\\{2,5,7,8\\}\\cup \\{1,3,5\\} \\\\  & =\\{1,2,3,5,7,8\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe union $Y \\cup Z$ is the set of all elements belonging to either $Y$ or $Z,$ or both. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y\\cup Z & =\\{1,3,5\\}\\cup \\{2,4,6,8\\} \\\\  & =\\{1,2,3,4,5,6,8\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe union $Z \\cup X$ is the set of all elements belonging to either $Z$ or $X,$ or both. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z\\cup X & =\\{2,4,6,8\\}\\cup \\{2,5,7,8\\} \\\\  & =\\{2,4,5,6,7,8\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157085 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157281 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "03cc876e-66d5-51af-ad8d-6c20bc599609" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unions of Sets Given Verbally"}] :question/id #uuid "6a3a434d-5fe4-53cd-ba34-4d10db5c85fe" :question/math-academy-id "e-7154" :question/problem "Let $A$ and $B$ be the set of all multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ and the set of all multiples of $6$ that are greater than $0,$ respectively. What is $A \\cup B?$" :question/worked-solution "The multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA = \\{ 4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32, 36 \\ldots \\}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $6$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB = \\{ 6,12,18,24,30,36,\\ldots \\}.\n$$\n\nNow, $A \\cup B$ is the *union* of $A$ and $B,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in either $A$ or $B,$ or both.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cup B & =\\{4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,36,…\\}\\cup \\{6,12,18,24,30,36,…\\} \\\\  & =\\{4,6,8,12,16,18,20,24,28,30,32,36,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157095 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37248a2e-6deb-5b4c-af42-51c358f21110" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Union of Sets Using a Venn Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "3de58ae0-eb3a-5faf-a404-0347d64d4979" :question/math-academy-id "e-7171" :question/problem "![](images/dc/dcddc9ee6fe49965ea4f261fcb43c6f7ccd14193910e864b950745ef513e67a6.png)\n\nThe sets $X = \\{ 1, 2, 3, 5, 8 \\}$ and $Y = \\{ 1, 2, 4, 8 \\}$ are shown in the Venn diagram above. Find $X\\cup Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The union $X \\cup Y$ consists of all the elements that are in $X$ or $Y,$ or both. To represent $X \\cup Y,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained within either $X$ or $Y,$ or both.\n\n![](images/c9/c94cfc38872dfe0673e112e09feec7781ab4f247f08932d1d8ecd167b4a99d32.png)\n\nThe elements $1,2,3,4,5,8$ are in either $X$ or $Y,$ or both. Therefore, the union of $X$ and $Y$ is\n\n$$\nX \\cup Y = \\{ 1,2,3,4,5,8 \\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554617 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37248a2e-6deb-5b4c-af42-51c358f21110" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Union of Sets Using a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cbb00e8-fa3a-5a23-a8f1-0bae0667c2ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{7,25,50\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553895} {:answer/id #uuid "2f08521a-3060-562d-954a-c40b0f5aa7e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{7,25\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553954} {:answer/id #uuid "4194f29b-c0cd-5734-a67d-babe2dbcf