either $A$ or $B,$ or both.\n\n![](images/79/7984b0cb81df816388aa0d5cbf860fc4bdad9f7e871e8671d4616ded02bcaf5b.png)\n\nThe elements $o,p,q,r,v,w$ are in either $A$ or $B$, or both. Therefore, the union of $A$ and $B$ is\n\n$$\nA\\cup B=\\{o,p,q,r,v,w\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554566 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65d40bd9-4d35-5e07-a767-8b2ae6ba559a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Union of Sets Without a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21ec46e2-7cea-500e-85fb-33a7017558ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{105,108,119,122,135\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553927} {:answer/id #uuid "23a4ac02-1db6-583f-82e6-b5db013364aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553931} {:answer/id #uuid "532eb7d1-8b72-50a6-be59-5e589c9d23de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{119,123\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554031} {:answer/id #uuid "916f172b-a98c-540e-998b-cf7c29a34a36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{105,108,118,122,135\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554185} {:answer/id #uuid "9f5952bf-4444-5543-a54f-4bae8c52221e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{105,108,118,119,122,123,135\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f5952bf-4444-5543-a54f-4bae8c52221e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{105,108,118,119,122,123,135\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554222} :answer-field/id #uuid "57364d10-fc9e-5cf0-a750-0891ce97fcf0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3ece29a0-cc0f-5be6-9001-b8cc96566290" :question/math-academy-id "q-102074" :question/problem "If $X=\\{105,118,119,123,135\\}$ and $Y=\\{108,119,122,123\\}$, then $X\\cup Y=$" :question/worked-solution "The set $X\\cup Y$ is the set of all elements belonging to either $X$ or $Y,$ or both. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X\\cup Y & =\\{105,118,119,123,135\\}\\cup \\{108,119,122,123\\} \\\\  & =\\{105,108,118,119,122,123,135\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554618 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157281 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "03cc876e-66d5-51af-ad8d-6c20bc599609" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unions of Sets Given Verbally"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f3ce74f-3cd9-5ddc-870f-ba877c7553c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{1,3,4,8,9,12,16,20,24,27,…\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553955} {:answer/id #uuid "69419d5e-cec8-59b3-9be5-476325804ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{3,4,6,8,9,12,15,16,18,20,…\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554075} {:answer/id #uuid "6d532b24-3d74-5a1e-9f87-6c1093e9a0ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{1,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,…\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554084} {:answer/id #uuid "d79beda6-776f-5231-b900-195a05c1e7fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{1,3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24,…\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554339} {:answer/id #uuid "fdbc25d6-14b6-50fd-a0ba-7e894e123ebf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{1,3,4,6,8,9,12,15,18,20,21,25,…\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f3ce74f-3cd9-5ddc-870f-ba877c7553c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{1,3,4,8,9,12,16,20,24,27,…\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553955} :answer-field/id #uuid "a097d8b4-61d7-5c24-b4fc-50630068161e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b7be71bb-2a94-5959-b6e1-bd279930afab" :question/math-academy-id "q-102147" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be the set of all non-negative integer powers of $3$ and the set of all multiples of $4$ greater than $0,$ respectively. What is $X\\cup Y?$" :question/worked-solution "The non-negative integer powers of $3$ are\n\n$$\nX=\\{1,3,9,27,…\\}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nY=\\{4,8,12,16,20,24,…\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, $X\\cup Y$ is the *union* of $X$ and $Y,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in either $X$ or $Y,$ or both. In other words, $X\\cup Y$ denotes the set of natural numbers that are either powers of $3$ or multiples of  $4.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X\\cup Y & =\\{1,3,9,27,…\\}\\cup \\{4,8,12,16,20,24,…\\} \\\\  & =\\{1,3,4,8,9,12,16,20,24,27,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554627 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65d40bd9-4d35-5e07-a767-8b2ae6ba559a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Union of Sets Without a Venn Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b45b2c-b1e5-51df-9233-681766e27744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{3,7,19,21\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553903} {:answer/id #uuid "4a7306b0-7e39-58dc-8d6a-5c02f3a160f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{2,3,4,5,7,16,19,21,22,115\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554014} {:answer/id #uuid "bf0053d6-a254-5c1e-99ea-5ee6dcb07e88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{2,4,5,16,19,22,115\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554284} {:answer/id #uuid "d9399757-788a-5b06-a74e-af23406c7392" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{2,3,4,…,114,115\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554343} {:answer/id #uuid "eae0bc31-6206-5abc-b4da-1a42e5fed347" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{2,4,16,22,115\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554381}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a7306b0-7e39-58dc-8d6a-5c02f3a160f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{2,3,4,5,7,16,19,21,22,115\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554014} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac450825-0a43-5655-9b1b-af418583e6b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554495}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e3ebe755-cc28-56a9-a6f9-b3ea716cdfc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-36187" :question/problem "If $A=\\{3,5,7,19,21,115\\}$ and $B=\\{2,3,4,7,16,19,21,22\\},$ then $A\\cup B=$" :question/worked-solution "The set $A\\cup B$ is the set of all elements belonging to either $A$ or $B,$ or both. So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cup B & =\\{3,5,7,19,21,115\\}\\cup \\{2,3,4,7,16,19,21,22\\} \\\\  & =\\{2,3,4,5,7,16,19,21,22,115\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234433 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157281 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "03cc876e-66d5-51af-ad8d-6c20bc599609" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unions of Sets Given Verbally"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42e85ab6-b6b8-5b56-a9f6-9a4f3ba83c4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answe